---
description: Stage 03 implementation planning constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

Stage 03 is in **implementation planning** until an explicit implementation gate is opened.

Design baseline **v0.7.5** (alignment candidate) under `artifacts/stage-03/` is the active planning input. Published baseline **v0.7.4** remains frozen in `artifacts/external-review/stage-03-design-v0.7.4-review.zip`. Do not edit published v0.7.4 artifacts during planning unless opening a new design release.

Forbidden during implementation planning:

- creating a canonical database;
- writing or applying SQL DDL;
- running ETL or loading clinical rows;
- reading or transferring patient rows for pilot execution;
- modifying raw Source A / Source B;
- modifying artifacts under artifacts/stage-01/ or artifacts/stage-02/;
- modifying approved Stage 03 Design artifacts or design-content-manifest.sha256;
- linking patients across sources;
- creating global_patient_id or global_subject_id;
- starting simulation or prediction engine work;
- promoting implementation-plan-report.md to FINAL.

Required planning invariants:

- first pilot uses Source A (`magerya_api`) only via read-only `mg_audit_ro`;
- derived target is isolated (`uhbse_canonical_dev.canonical_evidence` planned only);
- canonical IDs use HMAC-SHA256 with id_namespace_version 0.7.0;
- HMAC secrets are runtime-only and never committed;
- secret change without key_version bump is forbidden;
- provenance and temporal contracts from design baseline apply;
- quarantine is derived-only; raw data is never mutated.

When editing planning artifacts, update implementation-plan-manifest.sha256 via stage-03-implementation-plan-check.
